# Raw life-archive masters. These are the originals behind public/story/ —
# 860 MB of 192 kHz WAVs, 3264 px phone photos, and 55 MB video. Two exceed
# GitHub's hard 100 MB per-file limit, so they must never be committed. Only
# the optimized derivatives in public/story/ ship. Back these up elsewhere.
/src/assets/*.wav
/src/assets/*.mp3
/src/assets/*.mp4
/src/assets/images/20??-??-?? *.jpg
/src/assets/images/20??-??-?? *.png
/src/assets/images/2014-01-27.jpg
/src/assets/images/20??????_??????.jpg
/src/assets/images/1356462527318.jpg
/src/assets/images/1379461621138.jpg
/src/assets/images/2020.jpg
/src/assets/images/53j_5Zu_.jpeg
# iPhone originals behind the music-years photos, HEIC included
/src/assets/images/IMG_*.HEIC
/src/assets/images/IMG_*.heic
/src/assets/images/IMG_*.JPG
/src/assets/images/IMG_*.jpg
# iPhone originals behind the XR Lab, research and 2025 photographs. The screen
# grabs arrived as PNG and the .MOV clips are 4K — IMG_3942.MOV alone is 306 MB,
# three times GitHub's per-file ceiling.
/src/assets/images/IMG_*.PNG
/src/assets/*.MOV
/src/assets/*.mov
# Photos that came off the phone with a UUID or a Messages-export name rather
# than an IMG_ number. Listed individually because a glob broad enough to catch
# them would also swallow the project artwork in the same directory.
